b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & ⟹\\,x={y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/89/899357795c6d5b81d3cb619d71493ad787645697fe1f2fcecda78c1b875f388e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{3}\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0868f274-6d6e-5256-97a9-564c4f1a8169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186393194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "11bc950f-28ab-5ada-8524-78d17fbdb0fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c227960-e1d3-5f07-b75a-31b153d00a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186373174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52cd1fa6-d29c-562d-9d88-cade3cec5a66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd242e61-69b5-5bfd-bc83-d7379d3f45c8" #edb/ref 175921